<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Horn and East Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Ndorwa</h1><p class="st-meta">1600 CE – 1800 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A kingdom of the highlands between Rwanda and Uganda, remembered for its queen Kitami and as the cradle of the Nyabingi spirit cult.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Ndorwa lay in the hills of today's south-western <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/uganda">Uganda</a> and northern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-rwanda">Rwanda</a>. Traditions from the region describe it as a kingdom of the 17th century, linked by marriage and war with the Kingdom of Rwanda, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-mpororo">Kingdom of Mpororo</a> and the states of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-ankole">Ankole</a>. Its history is known only from oral accounts.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Little is known of its government. Traditions remember a queen, Kitami, whose spirit became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nyabingi">Nyabingi</a>, the focus of a powerful healing and resistance cult that spread across the region and later inspired revolts against colonial rule in the early 20th century.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Ndorwa broke up in the 18th century and was conquered by <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-rwanda">Rwanda</a> around 1800. Its lands were later divided by the colonial border between Rwanda and Uganda's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kigezi">Kigezi</a> district.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1600 CE – 1800 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Horn and East Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:91.54%;width:3.98%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1600 CE – 1800 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Traditional religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Rukiga, Kinyarwanda</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/rwanda">Rwanda</a>, <a href="/countries/uganda">Uganda</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Ndorwa</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1700&amp;focus=kingdom-of-ndorwa" aria-label="Kingdom of Ndorwa on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5517 2241 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Ndorwa lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5826 2522h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5837 2497h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5837 2497h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Rwanda. <a href="/atlas?year=1700&amp;focus=kingdom-of-ndorwa">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

